---
import ProjectLayout from '../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro';
---

<ProjectLayout
  title="Mortgage Approval Analytics"
  eyebrow="LARGE-SCALE MORTGAGE ANALYTICS"
  description="Turning millions of public mortgage records into a validated analytical dataset and an accessible interactive reporting experience."
  heroImage="/images/projects/mortgage-market-overview.png"
  heroAlt="Mortgage Market Overview Tableau dashboard"
  tools="Python · DuckDB · SQL · Tableau"
  metrics={[
    { value: '3.8M', label: 'raw HMDA records' },
    { value: '2.58M', label: 'completed lender decisions' },
    { value: '4', label: 'states' },
    { value: '3', label: 'Tableau dashboards' }
  ]}
  links={[
    {
      label: 'Open Tableau',
      href: 'https://public.tableau.com/views/MortgageApprovalAnalytics2017HMDA/MortgageMarketOverview?:language=en-US&:sid=&:display_count=n&:origin=viz_share_link'
    },
    {
      label: 'View GitHub',
      href: 'https://github.com/Ryan-Wenstrom-Portfolio/mortgage-approval-analytics'
    }
  ]}
>
  <section class="case-section">
    <h2>Problem</h2>
    <div class="stack">
      <p>
        Public HMDA data is rich but difficult to use at scale. The project
        focused on turning a large multi-state source into a consistent
        analytical table that could support clear descriptive comparisons
        across states, loan purposes, property types, income, and reported
        applicant characteristics.
      </p>
      <p>
        The goal was not to build a lending-risk model or make causal claims.
        It was to create a trustworthy, reproducible descriptive workflow and
        a reporting layer a nontechnical user could explore.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section">
    <h2>What I built</h2>
    <div class="two-col">
      <div class="detail-card">
        <h3>Validated analytical pipeline</h3>
        <p>
          Loaded California, Illinois, Michigan, and Texas records, standardized
          source fields, checked row and state totals, built the completed
          decision population, and exported an analysis-ready dataset.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="detail-card">
        <h3>Recruiter-friendly reporting layer</h3>
        <p>
          Published three Tableau dashboards covering market overview,
          property/income patterns, and reported applicant characteristics.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section">
    <h2>Pipeline</h2>
    <div class="pipeline">
      <div class="pipeline-step"><span>01</span><strong>Raw HMDA files</strong></div>
      <div class="pipeline-step"><span>02</span><strong>Schema + row validation</strong></div>
      <div class="pipeline-step"><span>03</span><strong>DuckDB / SQL transformation</strong></div>
      <div class="pipeline-step"><span>04</span><strong>Completed-decision table</strong></div>
      <div class="pipeline-step"><span>05</span><strong>Analysis + QA checks</strong></div>
      <div class="pipeline-step"><span>06</span><strong>Tableau-ready export</strong></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section">
    <h2>Selected findings</h2>
    <div class="finding-grid">
      <div class="finding">
        <strong>79.62%</strong>
        <span>Overall favorable outcome rate in the completed-decision analytical population.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="finding">
        <strong>80.45% vs. 78.10%</strong>
        <span>California and Texas favorable rates in the four-state comparison.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="finding">
        <strong>86.42%</strong>
        <span>Purchase-loan favorable rate, compared with 74.76% for refinance.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="finding">
        <strong>64.83%</strong>
        <span>Home-improvement favorable rate, lower than purchase and refinance in this descriptive sample.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section">
    <h2>Additional views</h2>
    <div class="stack">
      <figure class="supporting-visual">
        <img
          src="/images/projects/mortgage-property-income.png"
          alt="Property and income patterns dashboard"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption>
          Property and income patterns: descriptive comparisons across property
          types, loan amounts, and applicant income.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <figure class="supporting-visual">
        <img
          src="/images/projects/mortgage-applicant-characteristics.png"
          alt="Reported applicant characteristics dashboard"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption>
          Reported applicant characteristics: descriptive patterns by reported
          race, ethnicity, and sex.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section">
    <h2>Responsible interpretation</h2>
    <div class="note">
      <p>
        This project is descriptive. Differences in observed approval outcomes
        do not establish discrimination, causality, applicant risk, or lender
        intent. The analysis is not a fair-lending determination and is not a
        predictive credit model.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</ProjectLayout>
